  en: {
  baslik: 'Funeral Services',
  alt: 'What to do in the event of a death: the BDV Funeral Fund, the numbers to call, the step-by-step process and how to join the fund.',
  hizmetBaslik: 'Who is responsible for funeral services?',
  hizmet: ['Ritual washing (ghusl), shrouding, transfer to Turkey or burial in Belgium, and all official funeral procedures: the Diyanet Foundation of Belgium’s Funeral, Mutual Aid and Solidarity Fund (since 1982). In the event of a death, the fund is the first point of contact.', 'The mosque’s role: leading the funeral prayer, announcing the death to the community (mosque, website, WhatsApp), and organising condolence and mevlid programmes.', 'Our imam becomes involved once the deceased is brought to our mosque for the funeral prayer; he does not carry out the washing or the transfer.'],
  hizmetNot: 'No assistance is provided by the fund for funeral arrangements made without its knowledge. For the funeral prayer, please contact our mosque through our imam.',
  nakil: 'Death and transfer to Turkey →',
  acilBaslik: 'Numbers to call at the time of a death',
  acil1: 'BDV Funeral Fund — death line', acil1b: 'weekdays 10:30–12:30 and 14:00–17:00', acil2: 'Our imam — funeral prayer', acil3: 'Consulate General — duty line',
  surecBaslik: 'Step-by-step process',
  surec: ['Have the death certified by a doctor (death report).', 'Call the BDV Funeral Fund immediately: washing, shrouding, transfer or burial, and all arrangements with the funeral company are handled by the fund. If another company is used without the fund’s written approval, costs will not be covered.', 'Documents of the deceased to hand to the fund’s funeral company: the original Belgian residence card, the passport, the original Turkish identity card and the doctor’s death report.', 'If the funeral prayer is to be performed at our mosque, call our imam; the day and time are agreed and announced to the community.', 'The death is reported to the municipality (Marche-en-Famenne population department) — usually handled by the funeral company.', 'Transfer to Turkey: a Consulate transfer certificate plus a Saniport “laissez-passer mortuaire”, followed up by the fund and the funeral company.', 'If burial in Belgium is preferred: the multi-faith cemetery of Marche-en-Famenne/Aye (Muslim section), or Namur, Liège, Charleroi.'],
  karsilarBaslik: 'What does the fund cover?',
  karsilar: ['In Belgium: the coffin, washing and shrouding costs.', 'Transfer to Turkey: by air to the airport nearest the place of burial, then on to the place of burial in vehicles of the Turkish Diyanet Foundation and its partners; plus economy-class return tickets for two accompanying persons (one if several deaths occur at the same time).', 'If burial in Belgium is preferred: assistance of up to €3,000 against invoices; no ticket for accompanying persons in that case.', 'If the death occurs in Turkey: return tickets for two accompanying persons; the invoices must reach the fund within 3 months of the death.', 'Death outside Belgium and Turkey: where a Diyanet funeral fund exists in that country, it handles the procedures; otherwise assistance of up to €3,000 against invoices.', 'No expense made without the approval of the fund’s management is covered.'],
  uyeBaslik: 'Who can join, and who is covered?',
  uye: ['The file holder (head of the family): a Muslim Turkish citizen residing in Belgium. A person with Belgian nationality only cannot be the file holder; tourists and asylum seekers cannot join. Non-Turkish members who joined before 1 January 2005 keep their rights. Muslims from the Balkan countries belonging to Turkish and related communities may also join if they reside in Belgium (the transfer then goes to the airport nearest the place of burial).', 'Covered by the same file: the spouse by civil marriage living in the same household (even if not a Turkish citizen) and children under 18. Children in higher education remain covered for the duration of their studies; children with a disability of at least 3 points (certificate from the Belgian health authorities, renewed with the fund every five years) remain covered up to age 28.', 'A separate registration is needed for: dependent parents and parents-in-law; legally separated spouses; children aged 18 or over who have finished their studies.', 'If the head of the family dies, the spouse or another covered relative may continue the membership.'],
  kayitBaslik: 'Joining the fund online, step by step',
  kayit: ['Open the fund’s online registration form (button below).', 'Enter the file holder’s details: full name, place and date of birth, Belgian identity or residence card number, father’s name, mobile phone, e-mail, Belgian address and province, district and address in Turkey. The spouse and children under 18 are added on the same form.', 'Upload a photo of the front and back of the Belgian identity or residence card.', 'Read and accept the regulations; sign on the screen with your finger or the mouse.', 'After submitting, the screen shows the registration fee (it depends on age and is calculated by the form), the fund’s bank account and your personal structured communication (+++…+++); a PDF of the form and of the payment details is downloaded. Keep them.', 'Transfer the registration fee using this structured communication. You will be notified by e-mail that your application has arrived.', 'Membership starts 60 full days after the payment reaches the fund’s account; this waiting period does not apply to deaths caused by an accident.'],
  kayitNot: 'People officially moving to Belgium from another Diyanet funeral fund in Europe do not have to wait 60 days if they document their previous membership.',
  aidatBaslik: 'Annual dues',
  aidat: ['The fund’s management sets the annual dues each year; the payment letter is sent in the first week of January to the address the fund holds. If it has not arrived by 25 January, inform the fund.', 'Pay the dues within 10 days of receiving the letter and keep the proof of payment for at least one year.', 'Dues paid after 31 March are subject to a 30-day waiting period. A member with two years of arrears is covered again 30 days after paying the arrears and costs; a member with more than two years of arrears is considered to have left and must register again.'],
  degisiklikBaslik: 'Changes to report after registration',
  degisiklik: ['A newborn child: registered with your member number through the fund’s online «Spouse and child registration» form.', 'Adding a spouse: obtain a household composition certificate (composition de ménage) from the municipality, write your member number on it and send it to the fund by post ({adres}) or fax ({faks}).', 'Change of address: reported through the fund’s online «Change of address» form.', 'Marriage, divorce, the start or end of studies and similar changes must also be reported in writing in good time; the fund is not responsible for problems arising from unreported changes.'],
  cocukButon: 'Child registration form ↗', adresButon: 'Change of address form ↗', yonetmelikButon: 'Fund regulations (PDF, Turkish) ↗',
  kaynak: 'Source: Regulations of the Diyanet Foundation of Belgium Funeral Fund (V231019) and the fund pages on diyanet.be. Last checked: 23 October 2026. Amounts and conditions may change; call the fund for definitive information.',
  belediye: 'Municipal population department', mezarlik: 'Cemetery', fonSayfa: 'Fund information page ↗', faks: 'fax',
